    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nDot-repeating operation on visual selection does not repeat \"semantically\" when custom `<Cmd>lua ...<CR>` textobject mapping is used.\n\nThe behavior also changed in 2ac9dfc45dd5 (from what seems to be wrong one to the other wrong one).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create the following `init.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    _G.log = {}\n    _G.textobject = function()\n      local cur_line = vim.fn.line('.')\n      table.insert(_G.log, cur_line)\n\n      vim.cmd('normal! \\27')\n      vim.cmd(string.format('normal! %dGV%dG', cur_line, 2 * cur_line))\n    end\n    vim.keymap.set('x', '<M-m>', '<Cmd>lua _G.textobject()<CR>')\n\n    vim.api.nvim_buf_set_lines(0, 0, -1, false, { '1', '2', '3', '4', '5', '6', '7', '8' })\n    vim.bo.modified = false\n    ```\n\n2. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`\n3. Type `v` - `<M-m>` - `d`. This is meant to delete lines from 1 (cursor lnum) to 2 (twice cursor lnum) and it does.\n4. Type `j` (changes cursor lnum to 2) and `.`. This is meant to delete lines from 2 to 4, but it doesn't. On current `master` (and after 2ac9dfc45dd5) it deletes a single line. Before 2ac9dfc45dd5 it deletes lines 2 and 3. In both cases executing `:=log` shows `{ 1 }`, meaning that `textobject()` was not re-executed during dot-repeat.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nVisual dot-repeat always works \"semantically\", even when custom Visual mode mappings are used.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1551+gfdf071959e\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, doesn't have this functionality\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.2.3-arch1-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nFrom source",
