            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "When I tried to reproduce this, I found that it doesn't seem to be caused by `lua`. Even if using the command below to map key, the result is still the same as before.\n```\nmap <M-m> :execute 'normal! '.line('.').'GV'.line('.')*2.'G'<CR> \n```\nIncidentally, `vim` behaves the same way as `nvim` did before commit 2ac9dfc.\n\n",
